<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paglia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Paglia is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> that rises on Monte Amiata in southern Tuscany and flows through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umbria">Umbria</a> past the foot of Orvieto's tufa cliff to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a>. Its valley carried routes between Tuscany and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-francigena">Via Francigena</a> pilgrim road.</p></div>
